[Verification "Stockfish 18 NNUE checked; see accompanying report"]
[IntendedResult "win"]

{ No rooks left. Your pawns on e4, f5 and h7 face his on g4, but his king on f4 stands in their way. } 10... e3 { A sacrifice: your e pawn steps to e3, and his king has to leave your other pawns to take it. [%cal Ge4e3] } (10... h5 { Pushing h5 first gives him a capture. } 11. gxh5 { Lost: his g pawn takes on h5, and your pawns never get side by side. [%cal Rg4h5] }) 11. Kxe3 { He takes the pawn on e3, since leaving it would let it queen. } 11... fxg4 { Your f pawn takes on g4, and your g and h pawns are both free. [%cal Gf5g4] } (11... h5 { Pushing h5 before taking lets his g pawn capture it. } 12. gxh5 { Lost: he takes on h5, and your chance of two pawns side by side is gone. [%csl Rh5] }) 12. Kf4 { His king hurries back toward your pawns. } 12... h5 { Your pawns on g4 and h5 guard each other, so his king on f4 can touch neither. [%cal Gh7h5][%csl Gg4] } (12... g3 { Pushing g3 alone sends the pawn ahead of its partner. } 13. Kxg3 { Drawn: his king takes the g pawn, and your h pawn alone cannot win. [%cal Rf4g3] }) 13. d5+ { He pushes his d pawn with check, and now he has two passed pawns of his own, on b6 and d5. } 13... Kxb6 { Your king takes the b pawn first. [%cal Gc6b6] } (13... Kxd5 { Taking the d pawn lets his b pawn run. } 14. b7 14... Kc6 15. b8=Q { Lost: his b pawn queened on b8, right past your king. [%csl Rb8] }) (13... Kd7 { King to d7 blocks the d pawn and leaves the b pawn. } 14. b7 14... Kc7 15. Ke5 15... Kxb7 16. Ke6 { Only a draw: you caught the b pawn, but it cost the time his king needed to reach e6. [%csl Re6] }) (13... Kd6 { King to d6 stands in front of the d pawn, but the b pawn runs. } 14. b7 14... Kc7 { Only a draw: your king must run back for the b pawn, and his king gets time to deal with yours. [%csl Rb7] }) 14. d6 { His d pawn steps to d6. It is the last pawn he has in the race. } 14... Kc6 { King to c6, heading for his d pawn. [%cal Gb6c6] } (14... Kb7 { Also a win: b7 heads for the d pawn by another road. } 15. Ke5 15... Kc8 { Your king on c8 is close enough to take the d pawn. Still a win. [%csl Bc8] }) (14... g3 { Pushing g3 just hands his king a pawn. } 15. Kxg3 15... h4+ 16. Kxh4 16... Kc6 17. d7 17... Kxd7 { Drawn: all the pawns are gone, and two bare kings cannot mate. [%csl Rd7] }) (14... h4 { Pushing h4 lets his king take g4. } 15. Kxg4 15... h3 16. Kxh3 16... Kc6 17. d7 17... Kxd7 { Drawn: your pawns fell one by one, and you only got his d pawn back. [%csl Rh3] }) (14... Kc5 { King to c5 stands one step too far from the d pawn. } 15. d7 15... g3 16. Kxg3 16... Kb4 17. d8=Q { Lost: his pawn queens on d8, and your king never got to d7 to stop it. [%csl Rd8] }) 15. Ke5 { His king comes to e5 to guard the d pawn. } 15... Kd7 { King to d7, right in front of the pawn on d6. It has run out of road. Now watch. [%cal Gc6d7][%tail] } (15... g3 { Pushing g3 lets his d pawn go. } 16. Ke6 16... g2 17. d7 17... g1=Q 18. d8=Q { Drawn: a queen each, and neither side can win. [%csl Rd8] }) (15... h4 { Pushing h4 runs the race a move too late. } 16. Ke6 16... g3 17. d7 17... g2 18. d8=Q { Only a draw: he queens first, and your g pawn is still on g2. [%csl Rd8] }) (15... Kb6 { King to b6 steps away from the pawn. } 16. Ke6 16... g3 17. d7 17... Kc7 18. Ke7 { Lost: his king on e7 guards d8, and the pawn queens. [%csl Rd8] }) 16. Ke4 16... Kxd6 { Your king takes his last pawn on d6. Your pawns on g4 and h5 guard each other against his bare king, and the sacrifice on e3 made them. [%csl Gg4,Gh5] } 0-1


[Event "Lasker endgames: Give away the rook for stalemate"]
