{ You are a pawn down, so aim for stalemate: no legal move, not in check, and the game is a draw. Rook to c7. [%cal Yc8c7] } 1... Rc7 { Your rook stands on c7, ready to check along the seventh row. [%cal Gc8c7] } (1... Rxc6+ { Taking on c6 only trades the rooks. } 2. Rxc6 { Lost: he takes your rook with his, and his king and rook will mate your bare king. [%cal Rc2c6] }) 2. Rg2 { He swings his rook to g2, aiming at your back row. Offer your rook on d7, with check. [%cal Yc7d7,Rg2g8] } 2... Rd7+ { Check! His king cannot take on d7, because yours guards it. If the pawn takes, your king on d8 has no move: stalemate, and a draw. [%csl Gd8] } (2... Kc8 { King to c8 walks into a mating net. } 3. Rg8# { Mate: his rook seals the back row, and his pawn on c6 guards the squares beside your king. [%cal Rg2g8] }) 0-1


