{ You have a king and a pawn on c7 against his queen: hold the draw. The pawn is one step from queening, and his queen starts checking. } 1... Qb6+ { The queen checks from b6. Where does your king go? } 2. Ka8 { Into the corner on a8. If the queen takes c7 now, your king has no move: stalemate. [%cal Gb8a8] } (2. Kc8 { King to c8 stands in front of your own pawn. } 2... Kd5 3. Kd7 3... Qd6+ 4. Ke8 4... Qxc7 { Lost: his queen took the pawn on c7, and a bare king cannot hold against a queen. [%csl Rc7] }) 2... Qc6+ { He checks from c6 instead of taking the pawn. } 3. Kb8 { His queen covers a8, so b8 it is, and there your king guards the pawn on c7. [%cal Ga8b8] } (3. Ka7 { King to a7 leaves the corner, and the pawn falls with check. } 3... Qxc7+ 4. Ka8 4... Qd7 { Lost: the pawn is gone, the capture came with check, and there is no stalemate left. [%csl Ra8] }) 3... Qb6+ { He checks from b6 once more. } 4. Ka8 { Back on a8. The pawn on c7 is poison: if his queen takes it, your king has no legal move. Drawn. [%csl Ga8] } (4. Kc8 { King to c8 leaves the corner and blocks your pawn. } 4... Ke5 5. Kd7 5... Qb7 6. Kd8 6... Kd6 7. Ke8 7... Qxc7 { Lost: his king came up to d6, and his queen took the pawn on c7. [%csl Rc7] }) 1-0


