{ You are a pawn down: hold the draw. A fortress is a position he cannot break into, however long he tries. Build one: king to c4. [%cal Yd3c4] } 1... Kc4 { King to c4. His king on a6 cannot come out to b5 while you guard it. [%cal Gd3c4][%csl Gb5] } (1... Ke3 { King to e3 walks away from the a column. } 2. Kb5 2... Kd4 3. a4 { Lost: his king got out to b5, and now it walks the pawn home. [%cal Ra2a4] }) 2. a4 { His pawn steps to a4. Keep his king boxed in: king to c5. [%cal Yc4c5] } 2... Kc5 { King to c5 keeps b5 and b6 covered, so his king stays on the a column. [%cal Gc4c5] } (2... Kd4 { King to d4 opens the door. } 3. Kb5 3... Ke5 4. Kc5 { Lost: his king walked out through b5, and now it guards the pawn's road. [%cal Rb5c5] }) 3. a5 { The pawn steps to a5. King to c6. [%cal Yc5c6] } 3... Kc6 { King to c6, next to b6 and b7. His king still cannot leave the a column. [%cal Gc5c6] } (3... Kd5 { King to d5 steps back one square too early. } 4. Kb6 4... Kd6 5. a6 { Lost: his king got out to b6, and the pawn walks to a8. [%cal Ra5a6] }) 4. Ka7 { His king steps up to a7. Stay beside him: king to c7. [%cal Yc6c7] } 4... Kc7 { King to c7, guarding b8 and b7. [%cal Gc6c7][%csl Gb8,Gb7] } (4... Kd7 { King to d7 lets him out. } 5. Kb7 5... Kd6 6. a6 { Lost: his king on b7 guards the pawn all the way to a8. [%csl Rb7] }) (4... Kd6 { King to d6 steps back. } 5. Kb6 5... Kd5 6. a6 { Lost: his king on b6 shields the pawn, and yours is too far off. [%csl Rb6] }) 5. a6 { The pawn steps to a6. King to c8. [%cal Yc7c8] } 5... Kc8 { King to c8 keeps b8 and b7 under guard. [%cal Gc7c8] } (5... Kd7 { King to d7 drifts away. } 6. Kb6 6... Kd6 7. a7 { Lost: the pawn is on a7, and his king on b6 guards its road to a8. [%csl Ra7] }) (5... Kd8 { King to d8 is one square too far. } 6. Kb6 6... Kd7 7. a7 { Lost: his king on b6 covers the pawn, and yours on d7 is a step late. [%csl Rd7] }) 6. Kb6 { His king steps to b6. Go to b8, right in front of the pawn. [%cal Yc8b8] } 6... Kb8 { King to b8, blocking the pawn's road. [%cal Gc8b8] } (6... Kd8 { King to d8 walks off. } 7. a7 7... Kd7 8. a8=Q { Lost: his pawn queened on a8 while your king walked away. [%csl Ra8] }) (6... Kd7 { King to d7 leaves the corner. } 7. a7 7... Kd6 8. a8=Q { Lost: the pawn reached a8 with nobody in front of it. [%csl Ra8] }) 7. a7+ { The pawn checks you from a7. Into the corner: king to a8. [%cal Yb8a8] } 7... Ka8 { Your king sits on a8 in front of the pawn. If his king guards it, you are stalemated; if it leaves, the pawn falls. Drawn. [%csl Ga8] } (7... Kc8 { King to c8 steps out of the way. } 8. a8=Q+ { Lost: the pawn queens on a8, with check. [%csl Ra8] }) 0-1


